  m_text: "The Chipsets\r\n \r\nA chipset is a group of small circuits that coordinate
    the flow of data to and from a PC's key components. These key components include
    the CPU itself, the main memory, the secondary cache, and any devices located
    on the buses.\r\nA computer has two main chipsets:\r\nThe function of the northbridge
    is primarily a fast path between the CPU and the video bus and system RAM. While
    the southbridge connects with the slow hardware/components of the system. \r\n 
    Flow Diagram of two bridges:\r\n "
